## Severity Levels (Used in All Review Agents)

- CRITICAL — causes crashes, memory leaks, data loss, security vulnerabilities
- WARNING  — bad practice, technical debt, will cause problems at scale
- INFO     — minor improvement, style, optional enhancement

---

## Platform Conventions

### Android (Kotlin / Jetpack Compose)
- Architecture: MVVM + Clean Architecture (domain layer = zero Android imports)
- State: prefer StateFlow + collectAsStateWithLifecycle over LiveData
- Flag as CRITICAL: GlobalScope, !! force-unwrap, direct repository instantiation in ViewModel
- Compose: check remember, LaunchedEffect, derivedStateOf, collectAsStateWithLifecycle

### iOS (Swift / SwiftUI)
- Architecture: MVVM or TCA; clean separation of view and business logic
- Flag as CRITICAL: retain cycles in closures, force unwrap (!), unowned in async callbacks
- Concurrency: Swift 5.9+ async/await; flag missing @MainActor on UI-bound state
- Memory: weak self in all escaping closures that outlive the owner

### Flutter (Dart 3.x)
- All code must be null-safe; use const constructors wherever possible
- Never hardcode colors/font sizes — use Theme.of(context)
- State: match the project's declared state management (Riverpod, Bloc, Provider, setState)
- Always dispose AnimationControllers and other disposables

### React Native (TypeScript)
- Performance: useCallback for callbacks passed to list items, useMemo for expensive values
- FlatList: always provide keyExtractor and getItemLayout for fixed-height items
- Architecture: New Architecture (JSI/Fabric) preferred; flag synchronous bridge calls
- Avoid inline style objects in render — extract with useMemo or StyleSheet.create

### Unity (HLSL / ShaderLab / URP / HDRP)
- Mobile: ≤2 texture samples per fragment, use half precision, no dynamic branching
- Always expose tweakable values as Properties (never hardcode in shader body)
- URP: use HLSLPROGRAM; Built-in: use CGPROGRAM

### Unreal Engine (Blueprints / C++)
- Avoid logic in Event Tick — use timers, delegates, and event-driven patterns
- Cache GetPlayerCharacter() in BeginPlay, not in Tick
- Flag synchronous Cast To nodes inside Tick as CRITICAL performance issues

---

## File Naming Conventions

- Agent folders: kebab-case (e.g., code-reviewer, crash-analyzer)
- Agent files: always named agent.md
- Skill files: kebab-case.md in skills/<platform>/
- Prompt files: kebab-case.md in prompts/<platform>/

---

## Adding New Content

- New agent: copy templates/agent-template.md → agents/<platform>/<name>/agent.md
- New skill: copy templates/skill-template.md → skills/<platform>/<name>.md
- New prompt: copy templates/prompt-template.md → prompts/<platform>/<name>.md
- Every agent needs a real worked Example section — no placeholder output
- System prompts must be under 600 tokens
